Body:
This is still not officially supported, right? Or am I doing something wrong?

Thanks backkem for the workaround! But it seems you don't even need the custom provider. The following works:

```json
	"provider": {
		"openrouter": {
			"models": {
				"moonshotai/kimi-k2.6": {
					"id": "moonshotai/kimi-k2.6:nitro",
					"name": "Kimi K2.6 Nitro"
				}
			}
		}
	},
```

And regular OpenRouter auth config.

You can then either select that model interactively via `/model` command and select "Kimi K2.6 Nitro", or put `"model": "openrouter/moonshotai/kimi-k2.6"` into the config (root level).
